## N6: the detached-run mechanism, proven before the evidence run uses it
  Why this exists. The command tool kills a background task after roughly
  150 to 300 s and caps a foreground call at 10 minutes, and one full
  default run of the self-test costs about 17 minutes at full history.
  Three background attempts were killed at 167 s, 293 s and 143 s. The
  kills are the tool's limit, not the OS: memory sampled every 8 s through
  a run stayed between 18446 and 18539 MB available of 22015, the run
  never entered the top three by RSS, and a loop that allocates nothing
  was killed in the same window. The evidence run is therefore started
  detached (setsid, nohup, stdout and stderr to a file, stdin from
  /dev/null, disowned) from one short call and polled from later ones.
  This case proves a detached process outlives that window before the
  evidence run relies on it: a no-op that sleeps 400 s, then writes a
  marker. The probe's own output is copied here; no path is printed.
    detached probe
    start 2026-09-16T16:03:19Z
    marker OK
    end 2026-09-16T16:09:59Z
  marker lines 1, start lines 1, end lines 1 (expect 1, 1 and 1)
  N6 a detached process survived 400 s and wrote its marker: as-expected

